<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49676" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŭlū^brae</span></b> ,
			ārum, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small town of Latium</i>, <i>by the Pontine Marshes</i>, now <i>Cisterna</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 7, 18, 3</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 11, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 10,
				102</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 121
			sq.</span></i>—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŭlū^brānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Ulubrœ</i>, <i>Ulubran</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">populus,</span>”
				<i>the inhabitants of Ulubrœ</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 7, 12, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŭlū^brenses</span></b> ,
			ĭum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Ulubrœ</i>, <i>the
				Ulubrans</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 9, §
		64</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
